    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • Chinese Brand AITO Plans 2027 European Launch\n2027 Chevrolet Silverado 1500 Truck Production Underway at Silao Factory in Mexico\n33 photos\nPhoto: Chevrolet\nThe Silao assembly complex in Mexico spent four weeks down before 2027 model year Silverado half-ton pickups started rolling off the line. General Motors big kahuna Mary Barra and chief financial officer Paul Jacobson confirmed the news to investors during the Q3 2026 earnings call, adding that US dealers will get 2027s in the latter part of the fourth quarter.\nProduction at Fort Wayne and Orion is planned to start in 2027. As per Jacobson, production at Silao began at a measured pace. It will build towards normal output levels over the following months, which means that supply could be limited in the first half of the 2027 model year. Getting the line running properly before running it flat out is the less glamorous part of launching a new pickup, that's for sure!\nThe vehicle assembly complex in Fort Wayne, Indiana, should get its turn after some downtime beginning in December 2026, with 2027 Silverado 1500 production scheduled to start in January 2027. The Orion Township facility in Michigan will also build Silverado half-ton pickups, with Barra targeting the second quarter of 2027.\nOf course, the mechanically similar 2027 GMC Sierra 1500 shares the rollout. Beyond these facilities, General Motors allocated Silverado 1500 and Sierra 1500 engine production to a bunch of North American plants. Flint Engine Operations, for example, handles the 3.0-liter Duramax turbo diesel inline-six and small blocks.\nThe 5.7- and 6.6-liter V8 engines that replace the old 5.3- and 6.2-liter units also come from Tonawanda Propulsion and St. Catharines Propulsion. The final piece of the puzzle is the 2.7-liter TurboMax, a four-pot turbo gasser that is made in Spring Hill, Tennessee.\nAll 10-speed trannies are produced at the Romulus and Toledo plants in Michigan and Ohio. While final assembly occurs there, Bedford Casting Operations specializes in aluminum die-cast transmission cases, including cases meant for the 10L boxes used by the redesigned trucks.\nPhoto: General Motors Speaking to investors, Barra made it clear that General Motors focused on the stuff truck customers desire most in half-ton pickups. Think usable torque, predictable delivery, trailering and durability under load, as well as real-world fuel consumption. To ensure all that, Barra revealed that gen-six V8 small blocks had accumulated more than 100,000 hours on the dyno and over 1.6 million validation miles (or 2.6 million kilometers in metric speak).\nAlthough the 5.7- and 6.6-liter small blocks are the most anticipated engines for 2027, the Duramax soldiers on as one of the most interesting engines in the half-ton segment. Not only does it make the Silverado 1500 and Sierra 1500 unique in the segment, but over 900 miles (1,448 kilometers) of highway range is huge.\nSaid highway mileage when the diesel is optioned is only possible with the 34-gallon (129-liter) fuel tank. As far as Chevrolet is concerned, the shopping language has also changed for the 2027 model year. Instead of the LT, the Silverado 1500's middle trim level is referred to as the Silverado in advertising materials and media releases. That, however, is a bit misleading.\nFiring up the 2027 model's configurator, the midgrade is actually called LT when specified with rear-wheel drive or Z71 with four-wheel drive. Considering that Z71 goodies come standard when optioning four-wheel drive, it sure makes sense to call it as such. Barra also described how the High Country is moving closer to the materials, tech, and features you would normally associate with luxury SUVs.\nSuper Cruise becomes standard on high-end grades, with optional availability on lesser grades. Both the Silverado 1500 and Sierra 1500 support hands-free driving with trailering across more than 630,000 miles (over 1 million clicks) of compatible North American roads, especially highways.\nVia // GM\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nChevrolet Silverado 1500 2027 Chevrolet Silverado 1500 Chevrolet production 2027 GMC Sierra 1500 GMC Sierra 1500 GMC pickup truck\nAbout the author: Mircea Panait\nAfter a 1:43 scale model of a Ferrari 250 GTO sparked Mircea's interest for cars when he was a kid, an early internship at Top Gear sealed his career path. He's most interested in muscle cars and American trucks, but he takes a passing interest in quirky kei cars as well. Full profile\nUP NEXT 5 Fascinating Cars That Wowed the Crowds 40 Years Ago at the Paris Motor Show",
